# LOOP — social configuration (D52)
#
# LOOP has no build step. It is one index.html served as a static file, which
# is why it works in a basement and why it has no bundler to inject variables.
# These two values therefore live in the `LOOP_SOCIAL` object near the top of
# the social section in index.html — this file exists to name them, and to be
# the place a future build step would read.
#
# NEITHER OF THESE IS A SECRET.
#
# The anon key is designed to sit in a browser. On its own it authorises
# nothing: every table in supabase/migrations denies by default and every
# policy is written against auth.uid(). Security is row level security, not
# key secrecy.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key anywhere near the client. It bypasses row
# level security entirely. If it is in the bundle, every athlete can read and
# write every other athlete's data.

# https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
LOOP_SUPABASE_URL=

# Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon / public
LOOP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Leave both empty and LOOP has no social layer at all: no Friends entry, no
# network call, no behaviour change. That is the shipped default.
